		(uuid "16d777ab-d9aa-43e6-a1f4-73c6d4c373bb")
	)
	(text "Make sure to add header through holes in PCB to connect Line In/Out/GND to PCB\nUsing optional SD card/MEM chip pins.\nMake sure to free them if using in the future."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 365.76 132.588 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "2317ab94-1cfd-4996-bc5a-61ec290ba3d5")
	)
	(text "Storage\nFor 16-bit, total storage in Mb: (64 * Beats_per_loop * 10.584)/(BPM)\nFor some DSP like pitch shift/tape-stop, converting to 32-bit float helps, but recording as 16-bit PCM is fine.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 246.38 166.624 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "2b3f90cb-b197-4829-8429-be233492a183")
	)
	(text "Center positive"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 49.276 128.27 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "2b4251f7-b458-4a28-b4b5-74035b5ac5e1")
	)
	(text "AA_'NUM' means unused pins that are still connected to the Audio Adapter.\nThe Teensy and Audio Adapter board should be mounted directly on top of each other, per PJRC guidelines."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 307.086 32.258 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "48586e76-1231-4419-ab7a-e41f72cd674b")
	)
	(text "Pin 3 cap NEEDS to be rated 50V for headroom\nPin 21 is the exposed middle pad"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 518.668 157.734 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "668b6cb7-1a28-46b9-bfb8-5ed4d7b641b7")
	)
	(text "Likely will use U8g2 library instead of Adafruit 1306/GFX.\nSPI1 preferred so nothing weird happens with SPI0 (Audio Shield's SD/flash).\nIf low on GPIO, can move it to SPI0 instead, should be fine.\nLOOK AT RESISTORS, CHECK TO SEE IT'S IN SPI MODE."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 471.17 -71.628 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "670f92ed-b097-4304-8cf5-5e9203c9a649")
	)
	(text "Keep lines between Audio shield and jacks as SHORT AS POSSIBLE"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 427.482 33.528 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "726820ed-dd83-48bd-a16a-30fb963e8c91")
	)
	(text "In footprint:\nVBUS is A4, A9, B4, B9 tied together\nGND is A1, A12, B1, B12 tied together\nTVS to GND should be THE SHORTEST"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 416.052 152.908 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "7453ee90-648d-4733-b208-b934698439d4")
	)
	(text "A1/A2 ~4gb microSD card goes in Teensy's port, NOT the Audio Adapter's.\nKeep microSD internal. Expose file transfer via a separate MTP mode.\nDon't write 64 individual files. Group them somehow for faster speeds.\nTransfer via MTP, as WAV format\n2 APS6404L 8 MB PSRAM chips soldered on underside pads.\nCut VIN/VUSB\nMAKE SURE that total 3.3v output DOESN'T EXCEED 250mA"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 246.38 155.194 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "756b3dd2-c590-402c-a08e-cef2c2850124")
	)
	(text "FFC connectors/standoffs for connecting the 2 pcb's.\nSending ~16 data pins to bottom pcb\nRibbon cable needs to send multiple power/ground pins to distribute load (3/4)\nConsider high current from top board and noise"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at -52.832 7.874 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "822d24e0-4fcf-4ba7-acdf-4353cd80b34c")
	)
	(text "Not sure how to implement kill/off, or if needed\nCut VIN/VUSB, not sure which"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 145.796 126.238 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "a5ba8bb8-f745-4121-a425-926f38052b03")
	)
	(text "IO Expander ONLY if no pins left on teensy\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 24.892 -102.362 0)
		(effects
